% A constraint with comparisons: no reading may lie outside its sensor's
% range.  Variables used only in a comparison are bound by the positive
% literals, and every named variable is reported, in order of first
% appearance.
range(t1, 0, 100).
range(t2, -40, 40).
reading(t1, 50).
reading(t1, 120).
reading(t2, -41).
reading(t2, 0).
:- reading(S, V), range(S, Lo, Hi), V < Lo.
:- reading(S, V), range(S, Lo, Hi), V > Hi.
